today I'm going to show you a cocktail  called the ambrosial swizzle that I  created for clever clubs summer menu it  is pure refreshment in a glass the  ingredient list sounds a little long but  trust me it is worth it  you need some white rum strawberries  cucumber vanilla the cure  pineapple juice a little bit of lime and  a little bit of simple syrup and a few  dashes of bitters so we're going to  start by muddling some strawberry and  cue cover and simple syrup I think it's  really important to muddle with just  simple syrup or whatever your sweetener  is for one because sugar is a great  conductor of flavor but also if you add  all your ingredients and then try to  muddle end up bobbing for cucumbers and  stronger so just crush it up nice and  easy now we can have the rest of our  ingredients a little bit fresh lime just  half an ounce 3/4 ounce of pineapple  juice fresh if you have it can works ok  to 2 ounces of white rum 3/4 of an ounce  of vanilla liqueur a few dashes of  bitters bitters are an infusion of herbs  roots and botanicals and I like to think  of them as a spice cabinet they're not  meant to be the primary flavor but  they're there to enhance it so you just  need a little bit just a few dashes  alright so now we can shake this to be a  quick shake a couple of seconds we're  going to strain the string do a highball  or tall glass we're going to strain it  over cracked or crushed ice  so it'll melt a little faster so the  reason we didn't shake this drink very  long is because we're also going to  swizzle it a little bit with a bar spoon  swizzle is an alternative way to chill  down a cocktail it's very common in  tropical drinks you just rub your hands  together to move a spoon kind of like  you're building a campfire with sticks  it helps to dilute the ice and chill  your drink down alright finally slice a  cucumber it's a garnish there's a  regular at the bar that loves this drink  and he'll come in and say to me I need  to cool off and that's basically his  code for ordering and ambrosia swizzle  so the next time you find the heat  getting to you keep this drink in mind  if you liked this video and you're  looking for more tips to step up your  bartending game subscribe to the GQ  channel about lots more where that came  from
 

